    "Conclusion!B4": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "Reported EBITDA margin of 24% compresses to 1.5% normalised; reported PAT of ₹478 cr falls to ₹761.75 cr— a 60% compression. This arises from capitalising 89% of total interest (₹1,910 cr), inflating reported profitability. Normalisation adjusts for 50% of capitalised interest that should have been expensed.",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 20
    },
    "Conclusion!B5": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "Reported EBITDA margin of 13% compresses modestly to 12.4% normalised; PAT of ₹234 cr falls to ₹225.1 cr (4% compression). Interest capitalisation of only 11% reflects limited construction phase; metrics are largely stable post-normalisation.",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 15
    },
    "Conclusion!B8": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "SteadyInfra. On normalised basis, both have similar EBITDA margins (1.5% vs 12.4%), but SteadyInfra trades at 14.5x normalised P/E vs BuildCorp at 5.0x. BuildCorp's apparent P/E advantage is a mirage—once projects commission, normalised P/E will expand sharply. SteadyInfra offers stable, transparent economics.",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 25
    },
    "Conclusion!B11": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "REDUCE",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 10
    },
    "Conclusion!B12": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "Reported 8x P/E is a value trap. Normalised P/E of 5x is still cheap, but market has correctly discounted the 60% PAT compression that normalisation reveals. Severe margin compression (24% to 1.5%) is a structural red flag; profitability is construction-phase mirage. ₹20,800 cr CWIP will become depreciating assets within 24 months, depressing future earnings.",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 20
    },
    "Conclusion!B13": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "ACCUMULATE / BUY",
      "type": "text",
      "tolerance": 0,
      "points": 10
    },
    "Conclusion!B14": {
      "formula_pattern": "text_response",
      "expected_value": "Normalised metrics are already reflected in market price; 14.5x P/E is justified by stable ~12% EBITDA margins and minimal accounting distortions. Operational assets are earning cash; no illusion of profitability. Lower execution risk than BuildCorp. Steady dividend visibility.",
